      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That profound sense of futility you're describing is the core of deep compassion fatigue. When you see the scale of human struggle, it's easy to feel like your efforts are meaningless against the vastness of pain. Perhaps the \"point\" isn't in stopping the suffering, but in finding a way to make your own small moments of impact feel real, even if the larger picture remains overwhelming.",
      "source": "target",
